# The raid march (2026-11-08, the user's ask: "an actual film test in game of them coming out and marching"): a dead
# termite mound with a Matabele colony of 120 in it, a demo raid along a 40-block trail east (/antcolonies raid demo,
# set out the way the ribbon test does: the scout by the entrance, the rest in the rooms). Three cameras every other
# tick, so the three films line up: wide (the hump and the trail's first 20 blocks, fixed), side (riding along south
# of the column, a little behind the scout) and top (straight down over the column, east to the right). The trail's
# corridor is cleared of the mound's dead tree first, so nothing but the march is in the way.
#   ./gradlew runFilm -PfilmScene=tools/film/raid_march.film
#   python tools/raid_film.py     (the three films side by side: run-film/raid_march.mp4)
cmd time set 1000
cmd weather clear
lens 45
camera 0.5 -60 0.5 0 0
cmd antcolonies newmound dead 6
wait 200
cmd fill 14 -60 -6 54 -30 6 air
camera 6.5 -60 0.5 0 0
cmd antcolonies matabele 120
wait 100
camera 16 -46 22 155 16
wait 20
cmd antcolonies raid demo 40 east
cmd data merge entity @e[tag=raid_scout,limit=1] {CustomName:'"film-walker"'}
cmd tick freeze
repeat 450
follow off
fov 45
camera 16 -46 22 155 16
shot wide_{i}
follow -4 2.5 9 180 15
fov 50
shot side_{i}
follow -6 13 0 180 90
fov 60
shot top_{i}
step 2
end
quit
